{"id":"6075","groups":[{"type":"pnri","label":"相关图像","images":[{"src":"/images/compressed/6075_main_needle-ice_others.jpg","title":"","description":"<div class=\"img_desc\" id=\"desc1\"><p>土壤温度高于0 °C，但土壤上方气温低于0 °C，此时会形成<span style=\"color:var(--accent);font-weight:500;\">针冰</span>。次表层水通过毛细作用被带至地表而冻结。随着冰的增长，开始形成了这些<span style=\"color:var(--accent);font-weight:500;\">针状柱</span>。针冰的其它名称还包括霜柱。</p>\n</div>","copyright":"© Kevin A. Geiselman","location":"美国，宾夕法尼亚州，龟溪","latitude":"纬度: 40° 24' 21'' N","longitude":"经度: 79° 49' 30'' W","date":"02 January 2015 1452 (当地时间)","direction":"","cloudCode":"","code":"图像P/S代码: P.25.2","imageId":"图像P/S代码: P.25.2"}]}]}